resources.string:
The Degree in Informatics and Computers Engineering (LEIC) is one of the greatest degree in the "Técnico" and has already made a name for itself on the job market, both at national and international level. The LEIC graduates are recognized as competent professional with solid knowledge in the Informatics (Software Engineering) field and a good adaptability to the constant evolution of the Information Technologies.

 By the end of the degree, a student can specialise in one of the fields offered by the Master Degree in Informatics Engineering and Computers, on another similar deree or entre straight into the professional world.

\ The Master Degree in Informatics and Computers Engineering has its roots in the strong basis formation offered by the first cycle and provides attractive specialisations for students as well as serving as base for anyone who wants to entre a PhD program. It createsa solid basis for the intervention of the Informatics Engineering Department of the IST on the lifelong formation of students, which will represent an increasingly important component in the labour market of advanced education.

 By the end of the Master degree the students are able to entre the professional life. The students have a wide array of specific professional competencies, such as:
 - Analisys and project of complex systems;
 - Project and systems management techniques;
 - Modelation and data usage in information systems;
 - Application development for distributed systems;
 - Management, configuration and operation of computer systems;
 - Advanced techniques for problem resolution;
 - Adaptable systems projects, to solve complex problems;
 - Human inteaction projects that use natural interfaces;
 - Control and robotics;
 - Modelation and control of industrial systems;
 - Generic optimisation techniques.

 The typical employers for engineers that have their degree taken at IST are: service companies in the banking and insurance fields, software companies and telecommunication companies.
